description:
FOUND s513d (Opus, 2026-10-09) while giving lib/Scalar/Util.pm perl's prototypes (#2870).  PRE-EXISTING on main e969755e (code 26712581).

WRONG (loud here, silent when the invocant happens to have the method):
    use Scalar::Util qw(reftype);
    my $o = bless {}, 'K';
    my @m = (reftype $o, 5);   print scalar(@m), "\n";
perl 5.40.3: 2 (reftype($o), 5).  PCL: dies "Can't locate object method "reftype" via package "K"" -- the call became $o->reftype(5).  A sub DECLARED in the file (`sub mine ($)`) is right (2).  Probe: scratch/s513d/q/rt2.pl in the s513d worktree (perl 2/2; PCL 2/die).

MECHANISM: PExpr's indirect-object pre-pass skips a name only when `_is_known_callable($name, 1)` -- and the same-package mode reads declared_subs ALONE, never the prototype table, while an import (the module merge) registers a prototype record and no declared sub.  So every imported name is "unknown" to that guard.

FIX SHAPE: the same-package mode also accepts a per-package prototype record for the current package (positional, #2871: the record's site must be above the call) -- the one callable answer, rule 11.  Bar: guard rows (imported `($)` / `(&@)` / prototype-less list sub followed by `$var`), corpus-diff explained per file (the shape is common in CPAN code: `blessed $self`, `reftype $x`).


=== DONE (s513f) ===
_is_known_callable's same-package mode also reads the prototype record at this parse site (get_prototype) when it is an import (from_module) or this package's own -- `(reftype $o, 5)` is reftype($o), 5. Guard rows Pl/t/imported-term-01.t 19-20 (fail on main).
